{
  "abstract": "A Lean 4 and Mathlib proof that the matrix multiplication tensor ⟨9, 10, 11⟩ has rank at most 640 over the rationals. Two compared theorems: 640 triples of rational matrices decompose the tensor (∑ᵢ uᵢ[a, b] vᵢ[c, d] wᵢ[e, f] = [b = c ∧ a = e ∧ d = f]), and the same triples form a bilinear algorithm A * B = ∑ᵢ (∑ uᵢ[a, b] A[a, b]) (∑ vᵢ[c, d] B[c, d]) wᵢ over every field of characteristic zero. The scheme, scaled to integers, is data; Lean's kernel checks it (decide +kernel, no native_decide) slice by slice with the coefficients packed into large integers, and a soundness proof for every input turns the 90 slice checks, a range check and a bound check into the tensor identity. The smallest rank listed for this format in the Lille catalogue was 644 when this was written.",
